# Agent 2 Scope Rules

This repository implements Agent 2, which builds Antimony model
specifications from Agent 1's curated biochemical knowledge. See
`docs/01_agent2_architecture.md` for the full architecture.

## Agent 2 builds models only

Agent 2's job is: assemble the full biochemical network, assign
kinetic-law structures, declare/initialize parameters, assess module
boundaries heuristically, decompose the network into modules, build a
`ModelSpecification`, and generate Antimony (full and module-level).
Nothing else belongs in this repository.

## No literature curation

Never implement entity normalization, evidence extraction, claim
generation, confidence scoring, knowledge-gap detection, or experiment
recommendation in this repository. That is Agent 1's job
(`agent1-biochemical-curator`).

## No Agent 1 behavior duplication

Never import Agent 1's runtime package, ORM models, or database session
objects. Consume only `app.agent2.types.Agent1CuratedKnowledgeViewContract`
(`docs/02_agent1_handoff_contract.md`) — a local, decoupled representation.

## No Agent 3 validation beyond syntax/internal checks

Agent 2 may perform the minimal syntax/internal-contract checks needed to
emit structurally valid Antimony (e.g. "every referenced species exists in
this model specification"). Never implement mass-balance, conservation-law,
disconnected-subnetwork, or full unit-consistency validation — that is
Agent 3's job.

## No Agent 4 simulation/parameter fitting

Never implement Tellurium/COPASI execution, parameter scans, sensitivity
analysis, steady-state analysis, or parameter estimation/calibration
against experimental data. Agent 2 only declares and initializes
parameters; it may later consume calibration *feedback* from Agent 4, but
never performs the fitting itself.

## No Agent 5 critique

Never implement biological/model plausibility judgments — thermodynamic
consistency, cofactor sufficiency, ATP participation correctness, or
regulation plausibility. That is Agent 5's job.

## Do not silently expand scope

If a task or increment specification does not explicitly authorize
implementing network-assembly, kinetic-law, boundary-heuristic, module-
decomposition, or Antimony-generation *logic*, only extend the *contract
types* that describe it. Stop and report if broader scope appears
necessary rather than silently building it.
